{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwdirGaovCzQPLroubW3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its first run came back with status `ok`.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has one document per web request, with `timestamp` as the time field. Each request records:\n- the client IP (`clientip`), the URL and request path, and the response code (`response`, stored as text; I used `response.keyword`)\n- `bytes` transferred\n- source and destination countries (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`) and coordinates\n- user agent, OS (`machine.os`), referrer, file extension and tags\n\nThere are about 14,000 requests from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. The only response codes are 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441), so 503 is the only 5xx code present.\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-18545b28 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-18545b28-web-logs-overview-730e35074bf9`). It has 7 panels:\n- Total requests, Unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and Total bytes served, each shown as a single number\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and average bytes\n- Traffic by source country\n\nThe default time range is the last 7 days.\n\n**3. Rule: \"EFF-18545b28 5xx spike\"** (id `9f628ccc-abe9-43a2-bddf-a79d1eb76f2b`). It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that runs every minute. It counts requests whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" over the last 5 minutes and fires when the count is above 10. I tagged it `EFF-18545b28` and `web-logs`.\n\nThe rule has no action attached, so when it fires it creates an alert in Kibana but doesn't notify anyone. If you want notifications, a connector such as email or Slack would need to be added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":21757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":697},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"660ed580-85b5-4bc3-a4a3-18a9b463b8b9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:29:08.844Z","request_id":"req_011CfwdiqyxSyc7eMVUBJDYM"}
